From: 1582130940 <19632674+1582130940@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: bridge: enable tagged bridge NF by default on Airoha

Airoha PPE bridge offload relies on bridge netfilter seeing tagged VLAN and
PPPoE frames so firewall4 can create flowtable entries for bridged traffic.
The bridge netfilter module already defaults iptables, ip6tables and
arptables bridge calls to enabled, but keeps tagged VLAN/PPPoE filtering and
VLAN input-device preservation disabled.

Enable those tagged bridge netfilter defaults for the Airoha target so the
PPE bridge offload path is active without requiring LuCI to write sysctls at
runtime.

Signed-off-by: 1582130940 <19632674+1582130940@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 net/bridge/br_netfilter_hooks.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/net/bridge/br_netfilter_hooks.c
+++ b/net/bridge/br_netfilter_hooks.c
@@ -1249,9 +1249,9 @@ static inline void br_netfilter_sysctl_d
 	brnf->call_iptables = 1;
 	brnf->call_ip6tables = 1;
 	brnf->call_arptables = 1;
-	brnf->filter_vlan_tagged = 0;
-	brnf->filter_pppoe_tagged = 0;
-	brnf->pass_vlan_indev = 0;
+	brnf->filter_vlan_tagged = 1;
+	brnf->filter_pppoe_tagged = 1;
+	brnf->pass_vlan_indev = 1;
 }
 
 static int br_netfilter_sysctl_init_net(struct net *net)
